# The annotations of the mover $5000-$501F, the last 32 bytes of tape block 7: the source of src/mover/mover.asm
# (../../kit/mkgame.py --part src/mover/mover.json). Format: ../../../../docs/ann-format.md. Block 7 is code2
# (src/game, $5B00-$6AFF, assembled at its run address) followed by these 32 bytes; it loads at $4000, so the mover
# lands at $5000. Witness: c1 (work/stage1/c1), "L1 N" its run counts (work/stage2/counts.json).

@equ $4000 Screen 6144 ; the display file, where block 7 loads
@equ $5B00 GameStart ; code2's run address, the game's first byte (src/game KeyRows)
@equ $5B1B GameEntry ; the game's entry point (src/game Entry)

@module mover ; The mover: code2 from the screen to $5B00, then the game's entry
@about LoadGame in src/loader jumps here once block 7 is in. c1: entered at frame 16 279, T 8372; the game's entry $5B1B at frame 16 280, T 51 501 (docs/03-build-and-load.md 3.4, 3.5).

$5000 c MoveCode2 ; Copy $4000-$4FFF to $5B00-$6AFF and jump to the game's entry $5B1B
> Input: block 7 at $4000-$501F, the attributes black (LoadGame cleared them, so code2 in the pixel area is never seen). Output: code2 at its run address GameStart $5B00; the screen keeps code2's bytes until the game draws over them. c1: L1 1, the LDIR 4096 times.

$500F b MoverPadding 17 ; 17 zero bytes, the rest of the 32 the block carries; no code reads them
> c1: no L1 read. Kept as bytes.
